# Dev-only TOC, not for the client: exists purely so tests/harness.py can load the Modern
# conversion passes (tools/gen_modern_nodes.py, gen_modern_edges.py, gen_modern_abilities.py)
# against the real engine and see what breaks (see Data/Modern/CONVERSION_NOTES.md for
# what's still open -- riding skills, POI/service data, node names for anything not a
# renamed flight master or dungeon/raid entrance). Most of the engine's own files are still
# left out below on purpose: they'd load fine, since every one of them reads its data
# tables defensively (`addon.Edges or {}` and the like), but there's nothing for them to do
# yet, and listing them here would suggest more is wired up than actually is. Not a real
# per-ruleset TOC; see docs/DESIGN.md section 1 for what that will need
# (Mapzeroth_Mainline.toc) once the data conversion is far enough along to be worth shipping.

Constants.lua
Locales.lua
Locales_UI.lua
Options.lua

# Modern dataset (geometry only so far -- see Data/Modern/CONVERSION_NOTES.md)
Data\Modern\Containers.lua
Data\Modern\Nodes_EK.lua
Data\Modern\Nodes_Kalimdor.lua
Data\Modern\Nodes_Outlands.lua
Data\Modern\Nodes_Northrend.lua
Data\Modern\Nodes_Pandaria.lua
Data\Modern\Nodes_BrokenIsles.lua
Data\Modern\Nodes_Draenor.lua
Data\Modern\Nodes_DragonIsles.lua
